<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block">
  <!--
    MicronautPatterns.mml
    Declarative contract for reusable pattern recognition across Micronauts.

    This document defines data and authority boundaries. It does not register
    a runtime kernel, grant capabilities, or make a pattern match executable.
  -->

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>Pattern</mi><mo>=</mo>
      <mo>&#x27E8;</mo><mi>id</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>version</mi><mo>,</mo>
      <mi>matcher</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>captures</mi><mo>,</mo>
      <mi>scope</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>provenance</mi><mo>&#x27E9;</mo>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:micronaut-patterns:v1">PatternRecord</csymbol>
        <list><ci>id</ci><ci>version</ci><ci>matcher</ci><ci>captures</ci><ci>scope</ci><ci>provenance</ci></list>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
Pattern is a typed, versioned recognition definition. scope binds the pattern
to its Micronaut, field, phase, and context. provenance identifies its source.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>Match</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>&#x2192;</mo>
      <mo>&#x27E8;</mo><mi>bindings</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>evidence</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>status</mi><mo>&#x27E9;</mo>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:micronaut-patterns:v1">Recognize</csymbol>
        <ci>P</ci><ci>x</ci><ci>c</ci>
        <list><ci>bindings</ci><ci>evidence</ci><ci>status</ci></list>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
Recognition returns typed captures, match evidence, and a status. It does not
assert that a captured claim is true, select a plan, or authorize execution.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>PatternStages</mi><mo>=</mo>
      <mi>register</mi><mo>&#x2192;</mo><mi>normalize</mi><mo>&#x2192;</mo>
      <mi>match</mi><mo>&#x2192;</mo><mi>bind</mi><mo>&#x2192;</mo>
      <mi>compose</mi><mo>&#x2192;</mo><mi>emitCandidate</mi>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:micronaut-patterns:v1">PatternPipeline</csymbol>
        <list>
          <ci>register</ci><ci>normalize</ci><ci>match</ci>
          <ci>bind</ci><ci>compose</ci><ci>emitCandidate</ci>
        </list>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
Matchers may include literal, wildcard, typed-slot, n-gram, and relational
forms. Composition may map, filter, fold, or rewrite pure pattern data.
Every exported binding retains its type, scope, and source reference.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>{</mo><mi>unigram</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>bigram</mi><mo>,</mo>
      <mi>trigram</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>quadgram</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>supagram</mi><mo>}</mo>
      <mo>&#x2192;</mo><mi>candidateEvidence</mi>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:micronaut-patterns:v1">GramEvidence</csymbol>
        <list><ci>unigram</ci><ci>bigram</ci><ci>trigram</ci><ci>quadgram</ci><ci>supagram</ci></list>
        <ci>candidateEvidence</ci>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
Gram order describes sequence length and retrieval structure, not execution
authority. Corpus observations remain evidence. A framework is callable only
when a registered grammar/program contract validates and XCFE admits it.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>Legal</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#x2208;</mo><mo>{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>}</mo>
      <mspace width="1em"/>
      <mi>Utility</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#x2208;</mo><mi>&#x211D;</mi>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:micronaut-patterns:v1">LegalityUtilitySeparation</csymbol>
        <ci>Legal</ci><ci>Utility</ci>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
Candidate ranking may use relevance, corpus weight, learned preference,
attention, or critic evidence. XCFE legality is a separate hard gate and
cannot be outweighed by a high pattern score.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>Induce</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>context</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>observations</mi><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>&#x2192;</mo><mo>&#x27E8;</mo><mi>PatternProposal</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>structuralDelta</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>lineage</mi><mo>&#x27E9;</mo>
      <mo>&#x2192;</mo><mi>validate</mi><mo>&#x2192;</mo><mi>admit</mi>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:micronaut-patterns:v1">InductionProposal</csymbol>
        <ci>context</ci><ci>observations</ci>
        <list><ci>PatternProposal</ci><ci>structuralDelta</ci><ci>lineage</ci></list>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
Pattern induction may discover, generalize, specialize, or counterexample-test
a pattern in a new context. Equivalent candidates reuse an existing pattern;
a material, evidence-backed difference produces a versioned child proposal
with structural delta and parent lineage. Verification and authorized Xul
admission govern promotion; the pattern engine does not write learned state.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>CorpusBinding</mi><mo>=</mo>
      <mo>&#x27E8;</mo><mi>domain</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>keyPrefix</mi><mo>,</mo>
      <mi>corpusPath</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>micronaut</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>entryCount</mi><mo>&#x27E9;</mo>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:micronaut-patterns:v1">CorpusBinding</csymbol>
        <list><ci>domain</ci><ci>keyPrefix</ci><ci>corpusPath</ci>
          <ci>micronaut</ci><ci>entryCount</ci></list>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
Each CODEGEN expert corpus (data/gram/codegen-{domain}.jsonl) binds to a micronaut
via key_prefix namespacing: GramStore keys are stored as {prefix}:{bigram_slug}.
Domain→micronaut map: kuhul→CODEGEN-KUHUL-µ, cpp/h/hlsl→CODEGEN-CPP-µ,
py→CODEGEN-PY-µ, js/ts→CODEGEN-JS-µ, cs→CODEGEN-CSHARP-µ,
html→CODEGEN-HTML-µ, css→CODEGEN-CSS-µ, json→CODEGEN-JSON-µ,
khl→CODEGEN-KHL-µ, klsl→CODEGEN-KLSL-µ.
Loaded via GramStore::load_corpus() with 500K entry cap per domain. Corpora
are regenerated with tools/scrape.py --split --recent --max-per-domain 100000
to keep patterns stack-specific and recency-prioritized.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>Eligible</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>&#x03BC;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>op</mi><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>=</mo>
      <mo>{</mo><mi>&#x03BC;</mi><mo>|</mo>
      <mi>req</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>op</mi><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>&#x2286;</mo>
      <mi>cap</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>&#x03BC;</mi><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>}</mo>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:micronaut-patterns:v1">EligibilityGate</csymbol>
        <apply><subset/><ci>req_op</ci><ci>cap_mu</ci></apply>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
Eligible_µ(op) = { µ | requires(op) ⊆ capabilities(µ) }.
Eligibility gates before scoring. W·C·R never promotes an unqualified specialist.
Eligible_µ(op) = ∅ → capability_miss; dispatch_block_reason = MISS_capability.
CODEGEN experts are admitted only when the operator's domain requirement matches
their declared capability set. Cross-domain lookup requires an explicit
Bridge_alpha_beta admission; a corpus binding alone does not create a bridge.
Distilled question patterns (data/gram/codegen-distill.jsonl) contribute phase-tagged
evidence to the pattern pipeline but do not alter eligibility decisions.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <annotation encoding="text/plain">
MicronautPatterns contract invariants:
1. Recognition, interpretation, verification, selection, and execution are distinct.
2. Binding exports preserve type, context scope, and provenance.
3. Pattern scores are evidence, never XCFE permission.
4. Induced patterns are proposals until verified and explicitly admitted.
5. This MML document describes a contract; runtime support must be registered separately.
6. CorpusBinding key_prefix namespacing prevents cross-domain collision in GramStore.
7. EligibilityGate is a hard prerequisite; W·C·R scoring applies only within the eligible set.
  </annotation>
</math>
